            "role": "assistant",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "output_text",
                "text": "- **Perseverance has now driven a “marathon” on Mars.** NASA reported that the rover surpassed **26.2 miles (42.195 km)** of total driving, hitting the mark on its **1,890th Martian day (sol)**. An orbital image from **Mars Reconnaissance Orbiter’s HiRISE** also shows the rover’s route and tracks across the terrain.【5:0†source】\n\n- **Perseverance recently imaged Earth disappearing behind Phobos (a Mars “moon occultation”).** NASA published a new set of Mastcam-Z images where **Earth appears as a bright point of light** and then **vanishes behind the crescent of Phobos** (captured July 2, 2026; article published Aug 5, 2026).【5:1†source】【5:3†source】\n\nIf you tell me whether you want “latest” as *NASA official updates only* or *any outlet*, I can summarize the most recent items accordingly.",
